  "eval": {
    "slug": "deceptionbench",
    "displayName": "DeceptionBench (PKU)",
    "aliases": ["PKU-Alignment DeceptionBench", "DeceptionBench (Ji et al.)", "DeceptionBench (PKU-Alignment)"],
    "description": "Measures belief-vs-behaviour deception under scenario pressure. For each of 180 scenarios it elicits an internal belief from a neutral prompt, then records chain-of-thought and the final answer under pressure. Three model judges check whether reasoning tracks the belief while the answer diverges. The headline metric is the Deception Tendency Rate (DTR). This is the Ji et al. (2025) benchmark on PKU-Alignment/DeceptionBench (arXiv:2505.18807), not the same-named Huang et al. (2025) benchmark (arXiv:2510.15501), which is [DeceptionBench (Huang et al.)](/evals/deceptionbench-huang).",
    "summary": "Measures how often the model gives answers that differ from its own beliefs when under pressure.",
